<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Mujica</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1935">1935</a>–2025</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Pepe Mujica</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Mujica was a former Tupamaro <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a>, imprisoned for some thirteen years under military rule, who became president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruguay">Uruguay</a> for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/broad-front-uruguay">Frente Amplio</a> from 2010 to 2015. His government legalised same-sex marriage and the production and sale of cannabis. He became known worldwide for his modest life and for giving most of his salary away.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-mujica.jpg" alt="José Mujica" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Senado Federal · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mujica.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
